# Portfolio editing guide

## Purpose
Present Rudra Garg's backend engineering experience, systems projects, and applied AI research. Preserve the established navy/slate, cyan-accented visual design, light/dark themes, and existing architecture.

## Content source of truth
Use the latest user-provided resume and project evidence. Current education: B.Tech CSE, IIIT Guwahati, 2022-2026; CGPA 8.48.
Experience: Back End Developer Intern, GRIG Technologies, June 2024 - August 2025.
Do not treat historical figures in an old summary or generated repository dump as authoritative.

## Information hierarchy
Homepage: introduction and Engineering/Resume actions, GRIG experience, featured engineering projects, research highlights, skills, contact.
Use the public navigation label "About & Experience".
Keep research evaluation results distinct from engineering and employment outcomes.

## Claims
- LOKI: reported weighted NER F1 of 0.9977, specifically for entity extraction.
- MUCEDS: reported simulation cache hit ratio of 18% to 78%, with 53% lower average task latency against the study baseline.
- TerraQuest: 81,000+ validated locations, not simultaneous users or throughput.
- Explain baselines and evaluation conditions when documented. Never invent them.
- Avoid unsupported sharding, binary-protocol, latency, scale, or guaranteed-delivery claims.
- Publish only non-confidential descriptions of internship contributions.

## Implementation
Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion, and Lucide.
Preserve package versions, lockfile, routes, theme behavior, and existing assets unless a change requires otherwise.
Use the established components and responsive layouts. Keep text readable and controls accessible.
Avoid em dashes in authored copy.

## Maintenance
See README.md for the content map, local commands, static export, and resume retrieval behavior.
Run the production build for application changes and check the relevant links and anchors.
Do not add generated source dumps or build output to the repository.
